From ff940073aa8abe33ef511f79b8a44a09c7a4e178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:05:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add backend with SQLite database for sales qualification
 persistence
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turns the static localStorage-only prototype into a real app: an Express
server persists every qualification to a SQLite database (node:sqlite),
exposing a REST API the frontend now calls instead of localStorage. Sellers
can create a new qualification, work through the 6-step sales algorithm
with autosave per field, and return later to any saved qualification from
the home screen — all backed by durable storage instead of the browser.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
